    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "01. Core Concepts",
    "ruleNumber": "01.07",
    "summary": "For a **Battle-shock roll**, the unit’s controller takes a **[Leadership roll](vsdata:core-rule/leadership-rolls)** for that unit; on a fail, the unit and each of its models become **Battle-shocked**. A Battle-shock test means the same thing.\n\nA Battle-shocked unit:\n\n- has its models’ [Objective Control](vsdata:core-rule/profiles) modified to ‘-’\n- can’t be targeted by its controller’s [Stratagems](vsdata:core-rule/stratagems)\n- can’t start an **[Action](vsdata:core-rule/actions)**, or complete one it already started",
